## Architectural reference

TinyMCServer (https://codeberg.org/starclimber/TinyMCServer), AGPL-3.0, was
studied as the architectural reference for:
- downloading/extracting an Android/bionic OpenJDK into app-private storage,
- the foreground-service + WakeLock/WifiLock keep-alive approach,
- JNA/oshi handling for Paper-family servers on Android,
- the targetSdk=28 W^X compatibility constraint.

No TinyMCServer source code is copied or linked. JavaHost is an independent
implementation that generalises the approach beyond Minecraft.

## Runtime downloaded by the user (not included in the APK)

OpenJDK (GPLv2 with Classpath Exception) packaged by the Termux project and
downloaded at the user's request from Termux APT mirrors. The installed JRE
retains its `legal/` directory and the packages' own licenses. Nothing from
OpenJDK is redistributed in this repository or APK.

## Bundled third-party binaries

- `app/src/main/assets/jna/5.13/libjnidispatch.so` and
  `app/src/main/assets/jna/5.19/libjnidispatch.so`
  from the JNA project (Apache-2.0 / LGPL-2.1 dual license; the Android
  dispatcher binaries are Apache-2.0). https://github.com/java-native-access/jna
- `app/src/main/res/raw/silence.wav`: generated by the project (a 1-second
  near-silent tone), used only by the feature-flagged keep-alive test.

